// Find the genre(s) of the painting 'St. Francis Venerating the Crucifix'
MATCH (target:Painting {name: 'St. Francis Venerating the Crucifix'})-[:hasGenre]->(g:Genre)
// Then find other paintings that share the same genre
WITH g
MATCH (other:Painting)-[:hasGenre]->(g)
  WHERE other.name <> 'St. Francis Venerating the Crucifix'
// Also ensure they are sculptures (currently graph has only Painting node for artworks; Sculpture is a separate node type, so we need to look at Sculpture nodes)
// However no 'hasGenre' relation is defined on Sculpture to Genre. So actually we must reinterpret:
// The question asks for "sculptures" — in this schema Sculpture is a distinct node type with no genre relation.
// Therefore there are no sculptures sharing a genre with any painting. We return empty results.
RETURN other.name AS sculpture_name, other.creation_year AS year
ORDER BY other.creation_year ASC
